From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:23:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] system: fast-forward the guest clock and sound

Run the guest faster than real time, for skipping slow intros and grinding.

Every guest clock reading and timer deadline goes through ntimer, so the
speed is applied there: the teletimer reads
virtual base + (host now - host base) * speed, re-anchored at each change
so the clock never jumps back, and the timer thread sleeps deadline/speed
of host time. Tick counts, timers and the window server frame limiter
follow together.

Guest audio streams are paced by the host sound card, which would hold
titles that wait on their buffers at normal speed. The shared DSP stream
now takes speed times more frames per render callback and plays every
speed-th one: the sound is faster and higher pitched, and the guest
buffers drain as fast as its clock runs.

- config: fast-forward-speed (default 2, 1..8), the speed used while on.
- Qt: Emulation > Fast forward, checkable, shortcut Tab (works in
  fullscreen); off when the app stops; the status bar shows the speed.
- control API: GET|PUT /v1/emulator/speed {"speed": 1..8}, speed in
  /v1/status, fastForwardSpeed in /v1/config.

The phone clock runs ahead while fast-forward is on. Music played through
the MIDI/MP3 player backends keeps its normal speed.
